Every summary carries `product_sha256`, including a recompute's. Ruled (a) on
#68, 2026-09-11.

The digest is BINARY PROVENANCE and provenance is universal: a recompute
record was produced by a `diet` binary exactly as a drive record was, and the
ruling that made the digest mandatory at the boundary did not exempt one of
them.

It lived inside the drive's own variant until this fixture existed, and the
cost was not abstract. `check-results.py` requires `product_sha256` in every
results directory's front-matter and requires it to equal the summary row's --
so a directory whose record was a recompute could not be linted at all, and
nothing in the tree noticed, because `results/` held no such directory and no
fixture crossed the schema and the directory linter.

This is the fixture that crosses them. A recompute summary with every field
its kind declares and no digest of the product it produced is refused here,
by the same rule that refuses a drive summary without one.
